\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Morning comes with light all- cheering
\par Shades of night have fled apace;
\par Source of light, by Thine appearing,
\par From our minds all darkness chase:
\par Thou hast  blest us in our sleep;
\par Through the day direct and keep.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Earth refreshed Thy praise is sounding,
\par All Thy works Thy glory sing;
\par May our hearts, with love abounding,
\par Gratefully their tribute bring:
\par Thou hast taught the birds their lays;
\par Teach our hearts to sing Thy praise.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. All day long to praise Thee help us,
\par And to strive against all sin;
\par Finding all our help in Jesus,
\par Who for us the fight did win:
\par He was tempted here below,
\par And doth all our weakness know.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Man goes to his work till evening
\par Brings again the needed rest;
\par Grant that we, Thy grace receiving,
\par May in all we do be blest:
\par And wherever we may be
\par Find our joy in pleasing Thee.
\par                               Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
